    ],
    "turn_type_label": "Substantive"
  },
  {
    "episode_id": 43208,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43208.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "I think it's going to be helpful on many, many levels. First of all, this sports desert that we've been living through for a month, is maddening for those of us who are sports fans. So, you know, this is part of our lives, is therefore our team to follow the sports that we enjoy the most. So, this is a specific step in the direction of a return to normal state. It's also the case that Major League Baseball has developed a very extensive set of protocols to keep the players and the staff of their team safe. I happen to think they're going to be very successful. And when they demonstrate that that can be done successfully, it'll send a powerful message. So, you know, we can go back to mostly normal form of life. Right now, for those talking, there are a few tweaks to the rules. Things aren't exactly the same. The big difference, of course, is that fans won't be allowed in initially. But still, just the fact that we have a baseball season that means we're playing each other. It's a big step back in the direction of normalcy.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_08",
