  {
    "episode_id": 43208,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/3/43208.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "Now I didn't realize that before the roundtable just how sensitive these protocols are. I think it's a 120 page manual that they created scratch that contemplates all kinds of things that will be required to be tested every other day for the virus. Tested once a month for antibodies to the virus. There's all kinds of different rules that they're imposing on what happens in the clubhouse and how they eat their meals when they're at the stadium. So all kinds of things, it really was very expensive. The other thing that I think was very interesting is we heard from Reece Hopkins, the first baseman for the Phillies. And he left me with the distinctive question that the players have really bought into them. They understand this is serious stuff. They want to play. They're excited about playing. They're taking the protocols very seriously. They're complying with them because they know that by doing so, they keep one another safe. And I think that's a great attitude for them to have.",
